1. Purpose

The GhostHunter project is publicly available to encourage learning, collaboration, community contributions, and transparency in game development.

This license grants limited rights to use, study, modify, and contribute to the project while protecting the GhostHunter project and its creators from unauthorized commercial use.

⸻

2. Permissions

You are permitted to:

* View and study the source code.
* Clone this repository.
* Fork this repository on GitHub.
* Modify the source code for personal, educational, and non-commercial purposes.
* Build and play the game.
* Submit Pull Requests, bug reports, and feature suggestions.
* Share links to the official repository.

⸻

3. Restrictions

Without prior written permission from the GhostHunter Development Team, you may NOT:

* Sell this project.
* Sell any modified version of this project.
* Commercially distribute this project.
* Include this project in any commercial product.
* Charge money for copies of the game.
* Monetize the source code or any substantial part of it.
* Publish modified versions of the game outside GitHub.
* Rebrand the project under another name.
* Remove or alter copyright notices.
* Claim ownership of the GhostHunter project.

⸻

4. GitHub Forks

GitHub forks are explicitly permitted.

Forks may be used for:

* Learning
* Experimentation
* Personal development
* Educational purposes
* Preparing contributions back to the project

Public forks hosted on GitHub are allowed.

However, creating a fork does NOT grant:

* Ownership of GhostHunter
* Membership in the GhostHunter Development Team
* Partnership with the GhostHunter Development Team
* Commercial rights
* Rights to publish or distribute competing versions of the game

Forks should clearly acknowledge the original GhostHunter repository.

⸻

5. Contributions

Contributions from the community are welcome.

By submitting a Pull Request, patch, or any other contribution, you confirm that:

* You are legally allowed to submit the contributed material.
* The contribution is your own work or you have the right to contribute it.
* You grant the GhostHunter Development Team a perpetual, worldwide, irrevocable, royalty-free license to use, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and commercially use your contribution as part of the GhostHunter project.

Submitting a contribution does NOT:

* Make you a member of the GhostHunter Development Team.
* Grant ownership of the project.
* Entitle you to revenue sharing.
* Entitle you to royalties.
* Create employment or partnership.
* Transfer copyright ownership of the project.

Community contributors may be acknowledged in the project’s CONTRIBUTORS.md file at the discretion of the GhostHunter Development Team.

